<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">loot</ansi>

Battle spoils go into company cargo, with gold in the treasury.

  loot
  Collect eligible loot from corpses in your room, up to company capacity.
  Items that are too heavy remain. Gold does not use carrying capacity.

  loot own
  Collect only corpses claimed by your company.

  loot [corpse]
  Collect from one named corpse. get all [corpse] uses the same checks.

  autoloot on | autoloot off
  Optional automatic pickup from your claimed spoils after your battle ends.
  It starts off and never picks up another company's spoils automatically.
  If you cannot carry an item, it remains for manual pickup or more capacity.

Spoils are reserved for the winning company for 2 game hours, open to everyone
for 2 more game hours, then gone. Allies keep the rotating claim; outside one
alliance, the company doing the most damage wins it (ties: lowest player id).

No pickup or item use during battle. Loot contains actual drops, not gear that
stays with the body. Your allies' possessions and quest items retain the normal
ownership and item rules. A restart does not preserve runtime corpses.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help treasury</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help party</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.
